{"id": 39, "ts": 1779493125.283855, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I\u2019d like to summarize where we stand on the two leading candidates.\n- **Candidate\u202fA**: We have strong evidence of technical competence, anticipation of danger, spatial vision, and leadership. However, we still have **no data on his stress\u2011resilience**, which is essential for long\u2011haul flights. The lack of evidence leaves a critical gap that could outweigh his technical strengths.\n- **Candidate\u202fB**: Demonstrates reliable, conscientious work habits and **clear evidence of handling stress well**, making him the strongest alternative on that criterion. Yet, we have documented concerns about his **professional communication** (nasty remarks, pretentious tone) and a **weak numeric memory**, which could affect operational accuracy and crew cooperation.\nGiven these trade\u2011offs, I remain provisionally in favour of **Candidate\u202fA**, but only if we can obtain concrete observations of his performance under high\u2011stress scenarios (e.g., simulator debriefs, incident reports). Simultaneously, we should seek peer feedback on Candidate\u202fB\u2019s communication style to gauge the practical impact of his interpersonal issues.\nUntil we fill the stress\u2011resilience gap for A and better understand B\u2019s communication impact, we cannot reach a fully confident decision.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_2\", \"vote\": \"Candidate A\"}"}
